  "answer": "You can use the `lifespan` parameter of the `FastAPI` app to initialize and clean up shared resources. This can be done by providing a function that will be executed before the application starts up and another function that will be executed after the application finishes handling requests.\n\nFor example:\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.lifespan import Lifespan\n\napp = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)\n\n@app.lifespan_app_startup\nasync def startup():\n    # Initialize shared resources\n    pass\n\n@app.lifespan_app_shutdown\nasync def shutdown():\n    # Clean up shared resources\n    pass\n```\n[advanced/events-0]",
